# The ratchet's own prose heuristics.
#
# The six subjects in config.json are checks of the checker: each reproduces a
# defect this repository actually shipped, and each needs arbitrary computation
# (scratch corpora, merge simulation, PNG round-trips), so they stay scripts.
#
# This one is the other half of the argument -- a standing invariant that needs
# no plumbing at all, and so is written as data instead of as code. If the prose
# form cannot express the invariants of the tool that ships it, it cannot be
# claimed to express anyone else's.

heuristic test-suite
  run      node --test ratchet/dist/test/
  timeout  600000
  applies  when ratchet/dist/test exists
  measure  failing  number after "# fail"
  measure  passing  number after "# pass"
  rule     failing is 0
  rule     passing is at least 158
  because  a suite that shrinks silently is how a ratchet stops ratcheting: the
  because  count is a floor, raised deliberately, never lowered by accident

# The three below cover the class of defect the corpus was missing.
#
# Classifying the twenty-one v0 review defects against the six scripted
# subjects showed every one of those subjects was a check of a data structure:
# five of twenty-one defects, all in one row of the table. The other sixteen
# sat at the process boundary, on the CLI surface, in the capture-path routing
# or in packaging, and none of them had a subject -- because a scratch corpus
# and a deepStrictEqual cannot reach them. The corpus was built where it was
# easy rather than where the bugs live.
#
# Each of these runs a frozen instrument out of {home}, so `replay` and
# `adopt` measure every commit with today's driver instead of whatever that
# commit happened to contain.

heuristic cli-end-to-end
  run      node {home}/tools/e2e.js
  timeout  900000
  owns     .ratchet/tools/e2e.js
  applies  when ratchet/dist/src/index.js exists
  measure  failures  count of lines matching "FAIL "
  measure  declared  number after "scenarios declared:"
  measure  ran  number after "scenarios run:"
  rule     failures is 0
  rule     declared is at least 13
  rule     ran is at least 1
  note     each scenario names the guarantee it drives, so a red line is a
  note     sentence about the tool rather than a line number in the driver
  because  the loop in the README -- init, fmt, adopt, verify, break it,
  because  quarantine, reaffirm -- is the product, and running it by hand once
  because  per release is a ritual, not a mechanism

heuristic cli-errors-are-messages
  run      node {home}/tools/error-paths.js
  timeout  600000
  owns     .ratchet/tools/error-paths.js
  applies  when ratchet/dist/src/index.js exists
  measure  traces  count of lines matching "STACK "
  measure  silent  count of lines matching "SILENT "
  measure  homes  number after "broken homes:"
  measure  probed  number after "commands probed:"
  rule     traces is 0
  rule     silent is 0
  rule     homes is 3
  rule     probed is at least 8
  because  a stack trace means the failure reached the top of the program
  because  unhandled, so nothing decided what it meant, and the reader learns
  because  the line number of a JSON.parse instead of which file to fix

heuristic source-uniformity
  run      node {home}/tools/uniformity.js
  owns     .ratchet/tools/uniformity.js
  applies  when ratchet/src exists
  measure  violations  count of lines matching "VIOLATION "
  measure  declared  number after "invariants declared:"
  rule     violations is 0
  rule     declared is at least 4
  because  partial application of a mechanism -- defined once, wired into some
  because  of its call sites -- has shipped four times in three versions, and a
  because  corpus row cannot catch it: a row is one counterexample and this is
  because  a completeness property over a set of call sites
